JFtn
====

JFtn is a Java FTN node and tosser, derived from the original JFtn project.
Source and releases: https://github.com/vkravets/Fido4Java

Use the standalone ZIP distribution. It contains separate libraries, plugins and
editable Groovy mail scripts. Run jftn.cmd (Windows), ./jftn.ps1 (PowerShell), or
./jftn.sh (Linux/macOS) from the unpacked installation. A no-JRE package requires
Java 17 or newer; platform packages provide their own runtime.

The first start creates missing directories and prints a private browser setup
URL. Open the complete URL to create the administrator and station configuration.
For a manually configured node without UI/RPC, use jftn.conf.example, provide all
station/link settings and disable RPC explicitly. See docs/robot-access.md.

The default transport is Netty. Mail is stored in SQL, with optional JAM views
for external editors. Netmail and echomail are routed into durable outbound
packets; binkp acknowledgements complete deliveries. AreaFix, FileFix and directory
feeds are supplied as external scripts. The embedded browser UI supports English
and Ukrainian, light/dark themes, account security, node settings and outgoing
poll management. Browser mail readers are still planned.

Keep jftn.conf, conf.d/, scripts and all databases/mail/state together in backups.
Unpack upgrades separately and preserve operator configuration and data. Do not
replace a running installation or assume old database schemas are auto-migrated.

Documentation in the distribution:
- README.txt: launcher and directory overview
- docs/distributions.md: packages, upgrades and GitHub releases
- docs/web-ui.md: setup, sign-in, settings and UI tests
- docs/tosser.md: mail processing, routing, JAM and recovery
- docs/plugin-configuration.md: file-only plugin options
- docs/robot-access.md: robot rules and offline commands
- docs/rpc-ui.md: TCP/HTTP APIs and authentication

Original JFtn author: Dmitriy Tochansky.
Fido4Java maintainer: Vladimir Kravets.
